    "A": "Research exact serial top-k selection, keeping parsing unchanged initially. First measure a minimal optimization: once k entries are filled, reject points that cannot beat the worst retained entry before scanning the sorted array. Then compare a bounded max-heap, with O(N log k) worst-case work and O(k) selection storage, against materialized distance records plus partition-based selection with protection against quadratic degeneration. Order records by computed float distance, then original encounter index; the heap root must represent the worst pair. Equal-distance newcomers must not displace earlier points. Include an exact k=1 path. Select algorithms using general runtime properties such as N and k, never case identities. Preserve baseline behavior outside the optimized ordering assumptions. Deliver independently measured variants, explaining correctness, complexity, extra memory, and which improvement each measurement isolates.",
    "B": "Research input conversion, storage, and voting independently of selection. Replace repeated scanf calls with buffered input and correctly rounded float conversion, using strtof or an equivalently justified converter rather than approximate decimal arithmetic. Preserve valid signs, exponents, whitespace, label characters, and token handling across buffer boundaries. The query and k occur after all groups, so points must remain available until then; do not assume distances can be selected while initially parsing. Investigate fewer allocations or contiguous storage while preserving encounter order and an integration-friendly interface. Replace label qsort with a label-frequency table only if it preserves plain-char comparison order, repeated labels across groups, frequency ties, and any sentinel contributions. Measure parsing, storage, and voting changes separately where the existing measurement facilities permit.",
    "C": "Research CPU parallelism and data layout on the four-core ARM64 target. Evaluate contiguous, independently computed distance batches that permit vectorization without changing float arithmetic or contraction behavior. Where the unchanged build already supports threading, compare serial execution with at most four CPU execution threads. Partition points into balanced contiguous ranges, compute each range's exact local top-k using global encounter indices, and select the global top-k from their union; justify why locally discarded points cannot belong to the global result. Use private selection state and avoid shared heaps or per-point synchronization. Account for local candidate storage, merge work, and startup overhead, especially when k approaches N. Measure the distance-layout change and parallel selection separately. Retain a serial path when threading overhead or unavailable build support makes parallelism inappropriate.",
    "G": "Integrate only programs actually produced by A/B/C and validated through the unchanged correctness and timing harness. Establish the best standalone candidate before combining changes. Evaluate staged combinations: selection plus parsing, selection plus voting, then layout or parallelism. Remeasure every integrated program end to end; gains are not additive, and a combination may lose to either input. Preserve the fastest validated standalone program as a rollback candidate. Review equal-distance membership, vote ties, float evaluation, parsing equivalence, non-finite fallbacks, k>N padding, allocation bounds, and exact one-character output. Runtime dispatch must use legitimate input properties and measured general tradeoffs, not test identifiers or expected labels. Keep compiler, target, tests, oracle, permissions, and budgets unchanged. Report actual candidate identifiers, correctness outcomes, repeated timings, and integration regressions; retain the best validated result.",
    "analysis": "Only the supplied KNN program is in scope; A/B/C are research roles, not the other contest problems. The correct baseline averages 2.023236 seconds across three samples, ranging from 2.012756 to 2.034817 seconds, and passes four supplied correctness cases. No input dimensions or phase timings are available, so no bottleneck has been measured. Source-level opportunities are the O(Nk) neighbor maintenance, repeated scanf conversions, and sorting selected labels. Correctness requires the original float distance behavior, earlier encounter priority for equal distances, and the smallest label under the target's plain-char ordering when votes tie. Do not assume finite-distance ordering or k<=N without justification: retain reference-compatible handling for unordered distances and the baseline's unfilled -1 label slots when k>N. The plan separates selection, input/voting, and four-core execution so their benefits can be measured independently before integration."
